iMac 5K: put the stitched root plane in tile space before adding it

dm_update_plane_state() adds the root (left-tile) plane to the root stream
with the stock dc_state_add_plane() call, and the stitch layer narrows the
plane to the left tile only afterwards. But the add already builds the
scaling parameters: resource_build_scaling_params() clips the plane against
the root stream, which is one tile (2560) wide, while the plane still holds
the stitched-screen rects userspace submitted (5120 wide). If those rects
leave nothing inside x = 0..2559, recout and viewport come out 0 wide.
DCN tolerates that; DCE does not: dce_transform_get_optimal_number_of_taps()
only ASSERTs the width and then divides by it.

Seen on iMacPro1,1 (Vega 56, DCE 12), CachyOS 7.2.3 and 7.2.6, lean stack
plus the iMac Pro patches, KDE Plasma 6 Wayland: three hard freezes while
idle (2026-09-16, 10-06, 10-07), each the same trace:

  !(pixel_width)
  WARNING: dc/dce/dce_transform.c:921 at dce_transform_get_optimal_number_of_taps
  Oops: divide error: 0000 [#1] SMP PTI
   dce_transform_get_optimal_number_of_taps
   resource_build_scaling_params
   resource_append_dpp_pipes_for_plane_composition
   dc_state_add_plane
   dm_update_plane_state
   amdgpu_dm_atomic_check
   drm_mode_atomic_ioctl  <- kwin_wayland

The disassembly of the running module puts the return address on the root
add, not the peer add. The oops is in an atomic check with the modeset locks
held, so the display stays dead until a reset.

Narrow the root plane to the left tile before its add, with the same gate the
split already uses (stream_peer and a full-width fb), so the add sees the
final rects. A plane on a stitched CRTC that is not split (fb narrower than
two tiles) keeps its own rects; if they have no pixels on the left tile, fail
the check with -EINVAL instead of oopsing, and the compositor falls back to
composition. Either case logs the plane's clip rect (rate limited).

Applies on top of the lean stack (after the stitch layer).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -14262,6 +14262,7 @@
 
 	} else { /* Add new planes */
 		struct dc_plane_state *dc_new_plane_state;
+		bool stitch_split;
 
 		if (drm_atomic_plane_disabling(plane->state, new_plane_state))
 			return 0;
@@ -14310,6 +14311,41 @@
 		}
 
 		/*
+		 * Tiled stitch: dc_state_add_plane() builds the scaling params
+		 * against the one-tile root stream, so narrow the root plane to
+		 * the left tile before the add, to avoid a zero-width viewport
+		 * and a divide by zero.
+		 */
+		stitch_split = dm_new_crtc_state->stream_peer &&
+			       new_plane_state->fb &&
+			       new_plane_state->fb->width >=
+				       2 * dm_new_crtc_state->stream->timing.h_addressable;
+		if (dm_new_crtc_state->stream_peer) {
+			const struct rect *t = &dm_new_crtc_state->stream->src;
+			const struct rect *c = &dc_new_plane_state->clip_rect;
+			bool on_root_tile =
+				c->width > 0 && c->height > 0 &&
+				c->x < t->x + t->width && c->x + c->width > t->x &&
+				c->y < t->y + t->height && c->y + c->height > t->y;
+
+			if (!on_root_tile)
+				dev_warn_ratelimited(new_plane_crtc->dev->dev,
+					"TILED_STITCH: plane %d has no pixels on the root tile, %s (clip %d,%d %dx%d)\n",
+					plane->base.id, stitch_split ? "split" : "rejected",
+					c->x, c->y, c->width, c->height);
+
+			if (stitch_split) {
+				tiled_stitch_set_plane_rects(dc_new_plane_state, 0,
+					dm_new_crtc_state->stream->timing.h_addressable,
+					dm_new_crtc_state->stream->timing.v_addressable);
+			} else if (!on_root_tile) {
+				dc_plane_state_release(dc_new_plane_state);
+				ret = -EINVAL;
+				goto out;
+			}
+		}
+
+		/*
 		 * Any atomic check errors that occur after this will
 		 * not need a release. The plane state will be attached
 		 * to the stream, and therefore part of the atomic
@@ -14347,11 +14383,7 @@
 		 * when the stitch gate passed at crtc-state time, so its
 		 * presence (plus a full-width fb) is the gate here.
 		 */
-		if (dm_new_crtc_state->stream_peer &&
-		    dm_new_crtc_state->stream &&
-		    new_plane_state->fb &&
-		    new_plane_state->fb->width >=
-			    2 * dm_new_crtc_state->stream->timing.h_addressable) {
+		if (stitch_split) {
 			int tile_w = dm_new_crtc_state->stream->timing.h_addressable;
 			int tile_h = dm_new_crtc_state->stream->timing.v_addressable;
 			struct dc_plane_state *peer_plane = dc_create_plane_state(dc);
@@ -14369,10 +14401,9 @@
 				goto out;
 			}
 
-			/* Root plane -> left half; peer plane -> right half. All
-			 * rects (incl. clip) reconciled to tile stream space. */
-			tiled_stitch_set_plane_rects(dc_new_plane_state, 0,
-						     tile_w, tile_h);
+			/* Peer plane -> right half (the root plane was set to
+			 * the left half before its add). All rects (incl. clip)
+			 * reconciled to tile stream space. */
 			tiled_stitch_set_plane_rects(peer_plane, tile_w,
 						     tile_w, tile_h);
 			peer_plane->update_flags.bits.full_update = 1;
